# What `railway up` never uploads from this folder (gitignore rules: a leading "/" means the top of the project
# only, a name without a slash matches at any depth, a trailing "/" means a folder; names compare with case, hence
# the [xX] classes). Keep in step with .dockerignore. No "!" lines: scripts/deploy-ignore.ts proves with this file
# that nothing private leaves the computer (npm run deploy:check). Railway also reads .gitignore; this file does
# not rely on it.

# The case, the records, backups and anything set aside: never.
/[dD][aA][tT][aA]/
/[dD][aA][tT][aA].*/
/[dD][aA][tT][aA]-*/
/[fF][iI][lL][eE][sS]/
/[bB][aA][cC][kK][uU][pP][sS]/
/[sS][eE][tT]-[aA][sS][iI][dD][eE]/
/*.[bB][aA][kK]*
/*.[sS][eE][tT]-[aA][sS][iI][dD][eE]*
*.[pP][dD][fF]
*.[dD][bB]
*.[dD][bB]-*
*.[sS][qQ][lL][iI][tT][eE]*
[kK][eE][yY][rR][iI][nN][gG]*.[jJ][sS][oO][nN]
[kK][eE][yY][rR][iI][nN][gG]-[bB][aA][cC][kK][uU][pP][sS]/
*.[zZ][iI][pP]

